cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "A Component-Free Planar PCB Line Injector in a Business-Card Form Factor: Gerber-Based Prediction, Coupled-Inductor Measurement, and Bench Demonstration of AC Injection onto a DC Rail"
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-11-21
authors:
  - family-names: "Gautam"
    given-names: "Himanshu"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, India"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5291-496X"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - CERN-OHL-P-2.0
keywords:
  - line injector
  - PSRR
  - planar transformer
  - coupled inductors
  - air-core inductor
  - printed circuit board
  - open hardware
abstract: >-
  A printed-circuit business card of ID-1 size is designed as a
  component-free line injector. Two interleaved planar spirals form a
  1:1 air-core coupled inductor. Its self-inductance, mutual inductance,
  coupling coefficient, resistance and inter-winding capacitance are
  calculated from the Gerber files and measured with a handheld LCR meter
  and multimeter; the calculated self- and mutual inductances are within
  2 % of the measured values. In a bench test on a 5 V rail with a
  resistive load, the generator signal appeared on the DC side from
  100 kHz to 5.18 MHz. The release includes the paper, LaTeX source,
  Gerber and Altium design files, measured data, photographs, simulation
  files and analysis scripts.
